  "guide": {
    "title": "One programme, every event surface",
    "tracks": [
      {
        "label": "Build the programme",
        "steps": [
          "Open Edit programme to paste cells or import CSV and TSV. Review the column mapping, then add sessions or replace the programme. Unknown columns are kept.",
          "Arrow keys select cells. Enter edits and commits; Alt+Enter adds a line. Use the session form for dates, descriptions, links and images. Undo and redo work across table edits.",
          "Keep each Session ID and the Event ID when revising the event. Set End date for overnight sessions. Choose the event time zone and resolve any reported issues before exporting.",
          "Choose a screen layout and a look. Long titles travel at a readable speed, and scenes stay on screen long enough to show every word."
        ],
        "id": "build"
      },
      {
        "label": "Present and share",
        "steps": [
          "Choose Interactive page for a searchable programme with session details and calendar downloads. Export HTML for a standalone file with its fonts embedded.",
          "Use Reference time to rehearse Now and next. Snapshot videos hold event time; rehearsal videos advance it. Exported videos do not update live.",
          "PowerPoint offers editable text and shapes, or an embedded video with readable companion slides. Video playback support depends on the PowerPoint application.",
          "PDF and editable PowerPoint wrap and paginate full titles. If a still needs more than one page, choose PDF or HTML.",
          "Export ZIP for programme HTML, foyer and room screens, a scene contact sheet, PDF, poster and calendar. Include video in event kit adds a recorded MP4."
        ],
        "id": "share"
      }
    ]
  }
}
